      "body": "Fixes #7063.\n\n`procStat` in `internal/mcpclient` read `/proc/<pid>/stat` unconditionally, so process start-time identity (used by stdio handoff detach/adopt to tell a recycled pid from the original child) had no implementation on darwin, breaking the handoff tests and the darwin package build there (dezren39/nix#471 evidence via #237).\n\n## Change\n- `handoff.go`: the `/proc` implementation moves out; `ProcessStartTime`/`childAlive` keep calling the per-platform `procStat`. Start-time units are documented as platform-defined — a value is only compared for equality on the same machine.\n- `procstat_linux.go`: the existing `/proc/<pid>/stat` reader, unchanged.\n- `procstat_darwin.go`: reads the kernel record via `sysctl kern.proc.pid` (`golang.org/x/sys/unix`, already a module dependency): start time = `p_starttime` in microseconds since the epoch; zombie = `p_stat == SZOMB` (5, spelled out — x/sys/unix does not export it for darwin).\n- `procstat_other.go` (`!linux && !darwin`): explicit \"unavailable on this platform\" error instead of a doomed `/proc` read.\n- `procstat_test.go`: `TestProcStatSelf` — oracle is the kernel's record of the test process itself (exists, non-zero, stable across calls, not a zombie; a negative pid errors).\n\n## Verification\n- `go test ./internal/mcpclient/ ./internal/pool/ -count=1` on Linux (laptop): PASS (includes the handoff suites and the new `TestProcStatSelf`).\n- `pkgs/mcpx/scripts/darwin-compile-check.sh`: PASS — darwin/arm64 build of the whole module plus every package's test compile, 0 exceptions.\n\nCross-repo remainder (per #7063 acceptance): advance the mcpx pin in dezren39/nix so dezren39/nix#471's parked aarch64-darwin verification can resume — that step belongs to the nix repo and is named here as the follow-on, not done in this PR.\n\nQueue: task 12056 (repo-health-code-pilot), lane code-f.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796805335&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8008&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8008&signature=06d6db95f57d2cd03bc7fe856c5af7ad0a39237d86e6ab6a6a6b0703a4794f0d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8008?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Process handoff now reads process start times on Linux and macOS, helping distinguish a running process from another process that later reuses its ID.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * On other platforms, handoff now reports an explicit error when process start-time identification is unavailable.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
